{
  "_comment": "Nine time series characteristics: one stationary class and eight sources of non-stationarity. The label set is designed to answer two questions at once - is the series stationary, and if not, what causes it - so a flat 9-class model reports the hierarchy for free (any label but 'stationary' implies non-stationary, and the summed probability of the eight gives a calibrated non-stationarity score comparable against ADF/KPSS). No class carries a seasonal component: betise 0.4.0 seasonal bases sit at SNR 0.03-1.16, well below the ~3 that H1 needs to resolve a loop, so including them would add noise rather than signal. Seasonality is deferred to separate work.",
